1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,913
Pyre. Coins that build apps.

2
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:07,618
Write one sentence. An agent writes the spec.

3
00:00:07,838 --> 00:00:12,151
Stake 0.002 ETH, refundable, and it launches on pons.

4
00:00:15,551 --> 00:00:18,825
70% of every trade fee comes back:

5
00:00:19,045 --> 00:00:24,074
60 to the build budget, 25 to a $PYRE buyback, 15 to the launcher.

6
00:00:27,674 --> 00:00:30,668
At $50, an agent builds in a sandbox.

7
00:00:30,888 --> 00:00:34,899
Nothing deploys until the build, Lighthouse and a reviewer pass.

8
00:00:35,699 --> 00:00:40,103
It goes live on its own subdomain and charges in stablecoin. No gas.

9
00:00:40,903 --> 00:00:43,516
85% of revenue buys the coin back.

10
00:00:47,116 --> 00:00:49,146
Then it burns. Supply falls.

11
00:00:49,366 --> 00:00:52,674
Every burn carries an attestation anyone can reproduce.

12
00:00:57,116 --> 00:01:00,364
No budget, no agent. Any new fee relights it.

13
00:01:01,316 --> 00:01:06,698
408 tests, 58 of 68 production features, an independent security review.

14
00:01:07,748 --> 00:01:10,312
Pyre. Launching soon on Robinhood Chain.

